course: dictionary
lesson: 9298
title: Special: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word special has more than one meaning, so check the context. «It was a special day» means different from usual, often better or more important, like a birthday or a holiday.
explain: Special can also mean made for one particular person or purpose. «She wore special shoes for dancing» tells you the shoes were chosen for that job, not for every day. Ask yourself: what is special being used for?
explain: Special can be a noun too. On a menu, «today's special» is a dish or offer that is only available for a short time. Swap your meaning into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Special means different from usual, often better or more important.
fact: Special means made for one particular person or purpose.
fact: A special is a dish or offer available only for a short time.
fact: «Nothing special» means ordinary, not unusual.
fact: «Special educational needs» means extra help for some pupils at school.
exercise: «It was a special day, because it was my birthday.» What does special mean here? | Written down | *Different from usual, and important | Ordinary and boring | Very cold
exercise: «Clothes, colours and special marks are easy details to notice about a person.» What does special mean here? | Hidden under a coat | The same as everyone else's | Made of wood | *Different, so easy to notice
exercise: Ella sees «today's special» on the menu. What is the special here? | A kind of spider | *A dish or offer available only for a short time | A type of chair | A school subject
test: «Grandma bought special shoes for dancing.» What does special mean here? | Ordinary and everyday | *Made for one particular purpose | Wet and grey | Very heavy
test: Sam says «nothing special» about his lunch. What does he mean? | It was a special dish only on sale today | It was made of steel | It was the best meal he has ever had | *It was ordinary
exam: Which sentence uses special to mean made for one particular purpose? | «Nothing special happened at the park.» | «Today's special is soup.» | *«Snakes smell with their forked tongue, which carries scent to a special organ in the roof of the mouth.» | «It was a special day for the whole town.»
